# ArabGT Mobile — Project Memory

Car lovers social media and blog app (Flutter). Package: `arabgt_app`.

## Stack

- Flutter (Dart SDK >= 3.3.4), **GetX** for state management, routing, and DI (bindings pattern)
- **Dio** for networking (with curl/pretty logger interceptors); `http` also present for isolated cases
- Firebase per environment; OneSignal-style push and media via just_audio/audio_session
- Local vendored packages: `glass_nav/`, `scroll_date_picker-3.8.0/`, `packages/`

## Environments — IMPORTANT

Five environments, each with its own entrypoint, env file, and Firebase options under `lib/environments/<env>/`:
`local`, `dev`, `qa`, `stag`, `prod`.

- Run/build ALWAYS through a target: `flutter run --target lib/main_qa.dart` (same pattern for other envs)
- `env_<env>.g.dart` files are generated — never edit by hand
- **Red line: never touch anything under `lib/environments/prod/` without explicit approval**

## Architecture — feature-first clean architecture

Every feature lives in `lib/features/<feature>/` with this exact anatomy:

```
features/<feature>/
├── binding/          ← GetX bindings (DI wiring per route)
├── data/
│   ├── data_source/  ← API calls (Dio)
│   └── repository/   ← repository implementations
├── domain/
│   └── models/       ← entities/models
└── presentation/
    ├── controllers/  ← GetX controllers (business logic)
    ├── views/        ← screens
    └── widgets/      ← feature-scoped widgets
```

Shared code goes in `lib/core/` (`cache`, `data`, `domain`, `presentation`, `services`, `utils`).

**To add a feature:** replicate the anatomy above; register the binding with its route; controllers extend GetX controllers; API access only through data_source → repository — never call Dio directly from a controller or view.

## Conventions

- Follow `analysis_options.yaml`; run `flutter analyze` before considering any change done
- Feature folders and files: snake_case; classes: PascalCase; one widget per file where practical
- Existing in-repo guides to respect: `TESTING_GUIDE.md`, `MEMORY_OPTIMIZATION_GUIDE.md`, `TOKEN_MANAGEMENT_IMPROVEMENTS.md`
- App supports Arabic and English content — mind RTL in any UI work

## Red lines

- Never edit `lib/environments/prod/**`, `android/`/`ios/` signing configs, or anything under `env/`
- Never touch `_to_delete/` (pending cleanup — not part of the app) or `build/`
- Generated files (`*.g.dart`) are regenerated, never hand-edited
- All work happens on branches; PRs only — never push directly to protected branches

## Commands

- Analyze: `flutter analyze`
- Tests: `flutter test` (see `TESTING_GUIDE.md`)
- Run (QA env): `flutter run --target lib/main_qa.dart`

## Routing — central, three files (verified in code)

All navigation lives in `lib/core/domain/routing/`:
- `arabgt_routes.dart` — route-name constants (`ArabgtRoutes.*`) — add the constant here first
- `arabgt_navigator.dart` — `GetPage` registrations — register the page + its binding here
- `arabgt_go.dart` — the official navigation helper: **always navigate via `ArabgtGo.toNamed(...)`** (supports transitions) — never call `Get.toNamed` directly

New screen checklist: constant in `arabgt_routes.dart` → `GetPage` + binding in `arabgt_navigator.dart` → navigate with `ArabgtGo`.

## Feature-anatomy exceptions (verified — do not "fix" and do not imitate)

These features deviate from the standard anatomy for historical/practical reasons — leave their structure as is, and do NOT use them as templates for new features:
- `common` — shared widgets only (no binding/data/domain/presentation split)
- `casting`, `public_profile` — missing `binding`/`data` (and `domain` for public_profile)
- `dashboard`, `settings` — missing `data`/`domain`
- `interests`, `webview_html` — missing `domain`

**New features always follow the full standard anatomy** (see the architecture section above).

## Sentry (company org: `arabgt`)

- This app's projects, one per environment: `mobile-dev`, `mobile-qa`, `mobile-staging`, `mobile-prod`
- The backend has its own parallel set (`backend-*`) — never mix them up when triaging
- **Read-only phase**: reading and analyzing issues is allowed; resolving/assigning/modifying anything in the company org is blocked by guard until the team approves writes

## Branch flow (confirmed by Omar)

- Daily work happens on **`dev`** — feature branches fork from `dev` and PRs target `dev`
- Promotion chain for releases: **`dev` → `qa` (testing) → `staging` → `production`**
- Never commit or PR directly to `qa`/`staging`/`production` — they receive promotions only

## Linear (company workspace: ArabGT)

- Every ticket for this repo goes to team **ArabGT**, project **"ArabGT Mobile App"** —
  the company's SINGLE shared Linear project (mobile + backend use the same one).
  Never create or target another project.
- Sentry-derived cards carry the `Sentry` label so they stay filterable among regular tickets.
